            "review_title": "Review at MÌ CÁ HONGKONG 1988 - CN LÊ THỊ RIÊNG",
            "review_text": "Global62529396667\n5 contributions\n0\nFound a hidden Hong Kong-vibe gem on Le Thi Rieng\nJun 2026 • Solo\nYesterday we finished praising the other branch, and now we try the 115 Le City Private, the space here makes me surprise. The decoration of the classic Hong Kong vibe, the lights look extremely artistic, eat and feel lost in the old TVB movies, check-in every corner is sticky.\n\nAs for food, today I switched to cattle. The water is strong, the aroma of herbs is characteristic, the beef is soft, the beef is fattened and eats extremely.\n\nThe best part today is dessert: The High Spirit. I swear I recommend you try this! Lightly bitter and cool, eat with a little honey or super glue milk, eat this hot bowl of flour is the standard, heat up immediately.\n\nJust praised their other branch yesterday, and today I dropped by the one at 115 Le Thi Rieng. The space here totally surprised me! The decor has a classic, moody Hong Kong vibe with great lighting—it genuinely feels like stepping right into an old TVB drama. Every single corner is perfect for photos.\n\nAs for the food, I switched things up today and tried the Beef Stew Noodles. The broth was rich and savory with a distinct herbal aroma, the beef was braised to perfect tenderness, and the tendons were delightfully chewy and rich. Absolute perfection.\n\nBut the absolute star of the show today was the dessert: Herbal Jelly (Guanlinggao). Honestly, I highly recommend you guys try this! It has a pleasant, refreshing mild bitterness that pairs incredibly well with a bit of honey or milk. Having a cold jar of this right after a hot bowl of noodles is just the perfect combo to instantly cool you down.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten June 26, 2026",
